/*
:name: generic_default_attr_nil
:type: error
:error: default `Z\.\[bits\]` of generic `N` does not fold to a compile-time integer
:help: declared without bounds
*/

// User ruling 2026-09-27 (6): `.[bits]` of an UNTYPED comptime integer is
// value-derived, but a TYPED one keeps its declared type, and `Z:Unsigned`
// declares no width: `Z.[bits]` is nil (the body read agrees). A generic
// default that reads it cannot fold. It once reached the runner as a bogus
// type name, and a cassert over the call result then passed whatever it
// compared against.

comptime const Z:Unsigned = 13
cassert(Z.[bits] == nil)

comb width_of<N=Z.[bits]>(x) -> (r) { r = N + x }   // locate_error_here
cassert(width_of(x=0) == 7)
